globs: src/**/*.test.ts
description: Vitest testing style conventions for unit tests in this repo
---

## Vitest Style

- Import from `vitest`: `import { describe, expect, it } from "vitest"`.
- Name tests to mirror the API, e.g., `it('z.string().max(5)', ...)` or `it('z.enum([...]) rejects values not in the enum', ...)`.
- Use `parse` for success cases and `() => schema.parse(value)` with `.toThrow()` for failures.
- Prefer `toBe` for primitive equality and `toEqual` for objects.
- Keep one assertion path per test; split into separate tests when semantics differ.

## Structure

- Group related cases in a `describe` block per topic.
- Keep tests short and focused; avoid unnecessary comments.

